st - simple terminal
--------------------
st is a simple terminal emulator for X which sucks less.


Fork configuration and patch inventory
--------------------------------------
See PATCHES.md for the patch stack, personal configuration, and runtime checks.


Requirements
------------
The build requires Xlib, Xft, Xrender, Fontconfig, FreeType, HarfBuzz,
Imlib2, and zlib development files, a C compiler, make, and pkg-config.


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (st is installed into
the /usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install st (if
necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running st
----------
If you did not install st with make clean install, you must compile
the st terminfo entry with the following command:

    tic -sx st.info

See the man page for additional details.

Graphics
--------
This fork supports a subset of the Kitty graphics protocol, including native
PNG/RGB/RGBA images, direct and shared-memory uploads, and Unicode placeholders.
See GRAPHICS for usage, configuration, limitations, and the upstream source.

Run make check to exercise protocol replies and rendered pixels in Xvfb.
The checks require Python 3, Xvfb, and libX11.

